   <property name="text">
    <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Instructions:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Click the &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Finish Bottling&lt;/span&gt; button to complete your rum-making journey.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Did you know?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Bottling is the final step in the rum-making journey, preserving the flavor and character developed through fermentation, distillation, and aging. The type of bottle, label, and closure can influence how rum is perceived, both visually and aromatically. Many traditional distilleries take pride in hand-bottling, marking each batch as a symbol of craftsmanship. Once sealed, the rum no longer changes in flavor. It is ready to enjoy or age on the shelf.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Now hoist yer bottle high, ye’ve earned it; a fine brew worthy of any captain's toast!&lt;/span&gt; 🏴‍☠️ &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
   </property>
